  "interpretation": "At the reported family core diameter, the conditional stage shifts appreciably and model flux reaches 0.279 T, crossing the candidate B-H 0.2 T breakpoint. At 50/25 ns with a prescribed 200 ns base edge, it remains periodic and meets TP17 and solver-budget checks, but final EHT is about 12.38 kV (outside 11-12 kV) and retrace about 11.89 us (outside 12.8-19.2 us). The original 150 mm2 candidate meets both. Raising C27 through the inventory-supported +10% value (11 nF) and C30 to its +10% value (1.1 nF, if populated) still gives 12.154 kV and 12.091 us. A 15 nF C27 exploratory case passes both, but is 50% above its documented 10 nF nominal and cannot be selected as a .11 value. A5 needs a joint geometry, winding, loss and capacitance design check; this cross-revision diameter report alone cannot select the installed model.",
